// JPEG binary - Hello World! :: RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   colour     : not assigned by Linguist
//   layer      : full (byte-balanced rainbow bar)
//   upstream   : https://github.com/quxianp/RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   reference  : see https://esolangs.org/ and https://rosettacode.org/

# A JPEG opens with SOI, then a marker segment. A COM (comment) segment
# carrying "Hello World!" sits between them, so the greeting is in the
# file and the image data that follows is not needed to read it.
#
#   FF D8                 SOI
#   FF FE <len:2>         COM
#   48 65 6C 6C 6F 20 57 6F 72 6C 64 21
